#
# Counter-example for math:CollapsedMultiparameterFiltrationConstraint: a
# math:MultiparameterFiltration whose stages carry ONLY a single real
# math:filtrationThreshold and NO math:multiIndex — a nominally multi-parameter
# filtration silently degraded to the one-parameter case. The cross-node existence
# constraint (a multiparameter filtration must have at least one stage carrying a
# math:multiIndex) fires — shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (math:CollapsedMultiparameterFiltration).
# ISOLATION: the filtration IS complete for its frame — it names math:filtrationIndexPoset
# and a math:hasFiltrationStage, so math:IncompleteMultiparameterFiltration stays silent;
# there is no math:multiIndex at all, so math:DiagonalDegenerateFiltration cannot fire; the
# threshold quantity is well-formed (a dimensionless math:Quantity). So EXACTLY ONE finding.
# Back-reference: math:CollapsedMultiparameterFiltration (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecMultiparameterCollapse).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:collapsed a math:MultiparameterFiltration ;
    math:filtrationIndexPoset ex:grid ;          # completes the frame (poset present)
    math:hasFiltrationStage ex:stage .           # completes the frame (stage present)

ex:grid a math:MathematicalObject .

# The stage carries a bare one-parameter threshold and NO math:multiIndex — the collapse.
ex:stage a math:FiltrationStage ;
    math:filtrationThreshold ex:eps .

ex:eps a math:Quantity ; math:quantityValue "0.5"^^xsd:decimal .
<http://example.org/math/eps> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
